{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Submitted a review of artifact a34ce66287d643fa92eefaeb39ac7d58, the first artifact of obligation c-verify-leader-voter-quorum, which the trusted runner executed as check cc99cecfce9a453e81430792b77cee23 with checker outcome violated. Preflight returns valid:true. The product supplies the contract-required checker_correspondence item plus an applicability item, with no resolutions because no review issue is open for this target. Retained runner observation: verification_setup reported the leader as n2 with term 2, voters 2, nonvoters 1, quorum_size 2, other_voter n1, non_voter n3 and leader_state Leader; verification_observed reported other_voter_reachable false, verification_result success, an empty error, the leader still Leader and leader_stats_state Leader - so the leader confirmed its leadership on its own vote plus a non-voter's heartbeat while the voter majority was unreachable. The review argues the encoded predicate matches the obligation because the quorum VerifyLeader claims to confirm is the voter majority (r.quorumSize counts only Voter-suffrage servers) while the future is registered with every replication state, non-voters included, and each heartbeat success adds a vote; that the fixed entry is the module's own VerifyLeader and main loop with the shipped transport; that the oracle is the monitor comparison on the retained correlated events while the harness prints raw fields and exits zero; and that identity and ordering hold across the two events for the same leader. Alternatives are answered in the rationale: the leader genuinely still believes it is leader, which is the state the caller is testing rather than the confirmation the accessor promises; no source states a non-voter acknowledgement was meant to count; and the sibling lease check counts voters only, showing the voter-only basis this path omits. Limitations kept explicit: one non-voter and one unreachable voter only, the observable is the outcome rather than a downstream stale read, an unfinished verification is not distinguished from a failure by the predicate (and applicability was deliberately not conditioned on the result field, which preflight had rejected as filtering), and the leader is judged before lease expiry. Accepting this review should lift the blocker 'Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed' and make this the tenth confirmed in-scope finding, on the consensus-safety side rather than the client-contract side. About 15 minutes and 2 audit units remain.\"}"}}
